<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anglo-Spanish War (1585–1604)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1585">1585</a>–<a href="/years/1604">1604</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Anglo-Spanish War of 1585–1604 was an undeclared war between Elizabethan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, provoked by English support for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-revolt">Dutch Revolt</a> and English privateering against Spanish shipping. Its best-known episode was the defeat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-armada">Spanish Armada</a> in 1588, while later expeditions on both sides, including the English Armada of 1589 and Spanish landings in Ireland, achieved little. The Treaty of London (1604) restored peace under James I.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/anglo-spanish-war-1585-1604.jpg" alt="Anglo-Spanish War (1585–1604)" width="320" height="250" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: anonymous · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:English_Ships_and_the_Spanish_Armada,_August_1588_RMG_BHC0262.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
